{"id":"int-aafc03a58e13dfe6672225cd9cd0ce35","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-31T13:44:00.3866601Z","actor":"Chad Walker","issue_id":"repo-diy","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"blocked","reason":"Superseded by repo-zje, which narrows it against a testability assessment. Two criteria were dropped as uncheckable without Docker ('a suite passes identically standalone and inside the sweep' is a host obligation, not a frozen test), and the shape changed: ownership becomes a before/after snapshot diff intersected with an allowlist, driven through a single SWEEP_DOCKER seam so the whole thing is Docker-free. repo-zje also carries a live bug this issue did not know about: three suites filter on docker's name=task-, which is a SUBSTRING match, so an unrelated host container named my-task-runner is force-removed."}}
